def merge_sort(nums):
    if len(nums) <= 1:
        return nums
    mid = len(nums) // 2
    left = merge_sort(nums[:mid])
    right = merge_sort(nums[mid:])
    return merge(left, right)
print(merge_sort([38, 27, 43, 3, 9]))  # [3, 9, 27, 38, 43]
merge is the function from the merging topic. Trust the recursive calls to return sorted halves.

